# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Issuance material — must never reach history
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `codes_export_*.txt` holds the plaintext of every activation code in a batch.
# Committing it would put 500 working licence keys into the repository and into
# every clone and fork of it, where they could not be recalled — the same class
# of mistake as committing a private key. `issue.rs` writes it beside the
# ledger, which is inside the repo, so this rule is the only thing standing
# between a routine `git add -A` and a shipped-secret incident.
src-tauri/codes_export_*.txt

# The ledger itself is deliberately NOT ignored: it stores only hashes, so it is
# safe to version and useful to — it records which codes exist, which are spent,
# and on which device. Only `mark`'s transient backup is excluded.
src-tauri/license_inventory.csv.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verification scratch space
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `_tmp/` is the harness's output directory: 30 screenshots per run, plus the
# ad-hoc `ui-dump.mjs` and the vite logs. All of it is regenerated by running
# `node tools/ui-verify.mjs`, so none of it belongs in history — it would add
# several MB per commit and produce diff noise on every run.
_tmp/

# `tools/fixtures.json` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is an 880 KB capture of
# real Tauri command payloads, and it cannot currently be regenerated: the
# `cargo run --bin probe` that the harness error message refers to does not
# exist in this tree. Committing it is what makes the harness reproducible on a
# clean checkout; ignoring it would silently reduce every UI assertion to a
# failure on first run.

